{"id":132714776717751,"type":"album","name":"Confield","artist":"Autechre","year":2001,"weight":14,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/confield-1.jpg","aoty":72,"aoty_user":82,"yt":"ikRwIH9tjKM","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/autechre/confield","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/1512-autechre-confield.php"},"desc":"With Confield, Sean Booth and Rob Brown largely abandoned the warm ambient sounds of their earlier works such as Amber and Tri Repetae in favour of the more chaotic feel that they had been pursuing with LP5, EP7, and Peel Session. Confield saw the experimental use of computer programs to form the basis of songs instead of stand-alone synthesizers. According to Booth, \"Most of Confield came out of experiments with Max that weren't really applicable in a club environment.\" One of the more controversial aspects of the album's production was, like EP7, the use of generative sequences for certain aspects ."},"artist_ref":{"id":239368523925436,"name":"Autechre","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Autechre1.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":184262862830389,"type":"genre","name":"IDM","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":387,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":66816368646126,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — IDM","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":8,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":150848509715573,"name":"RYM Top — Experimental","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":26,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":15302027328081,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":76,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":44735175437010,"name":"AOTY Must Hear 2000s","src":"charts","grp":"AOTY","list_year":null,"rank":463,"year":2001,"note":null,"total":520,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[],"book_tracks":[{"